<%#
  Phase 8: only fixed, server-controlled property names
  (LocalDesign::Design::CSS_VARIABLES) are ever printed on the left of a
  `:` — never a user-provided string — and only values that already passed
  LocalDesignSetting's `RGB_HEX_FORMAT` validation are printed on the right,
  each still run through `sanitize_hex` (belt-and-suspenders: this partial
  must never trust that every past/future write path revalidated). No
  `html_safe`/`raw` on anything user-influenced.
%>
<% setting = LocalDesignSetting.current %>
<style type="text/css">
  :root {
    <% setting.effective_colors.each do |key, value| %>
      <%= LocalDesign::Design.css_variable_for(key) %>: <%= sanitize_hex(value) %>;
    <% end %>
  }

  <%#
    The five variables below did not exist in v17.6.0 (see
    LocalDesign::Design::NEWLY_INTRODUCED_VARIABLE_KEYS) so, unlike the ten
    above, setting them alone has no visual effect — these small rules are
    what actually consumes them. They are a best-effort, conservatively
    scoped mapping onto the closest existing OpenProject selectors found in
    frontend/src/global_styles at analysis time, not a guarantee of
    pixel-perfect parity with every hover state in the app (some hover
    feedback is applied via JS-toggled classes rather than native `:hover`,
    which a CSS-only rule cannot reach) — see docs/local-design/testing.md,
    "Known limitations", for the full caveat. Reused variables (the other
    ten) have no such limitation: they plug directly into selectors that
    already exist.
  %>
  .op-uc-container a {
    color: var(--op-local-design-link-color);
  }
  .op-uc-container a:hover {
    color: var(--op-local-design-link-hover-color);
  }
  .op-app-header a:hover,
  .op-app-header button:hover {
    background-color: var(--op-local-design-header-hover-background);
  }
  #main-menu a:hover {
    background-color: var(--op-local-design-main-menu-hover-background);
  }
  :focus-visible {
    outline-color: var(--op-local-design-focus-indicator-color);
  }
</style>
